1
00:04:08,919 --> 00:04:10,360
It's—it's recording now?

2
00:04:10,879 --> 00:04:11,479
Yeah, it's recording.

3
00:04:11,479 --> 00:04:12,120
Cao Jun.

4
00:04:13,039 --> 00:04:13,360
Well...

5
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:14,800
How about I drive a lap for you?

6
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:15,639
No need, no need.

7
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:16,759
Just stay seated.

8
00:04:17,079 --> 00:04:17,560
All right.

9
00:04:19,680 --> 00:04:21,279
Your plant had a drinking contest yesterday.

10
00:04:21,319 --> 00:04:22,240
How come you didn't go?

11
00:04:23,399 --> 00:04:24,279
I'm no good at drinking.

12
00:04:24,319 --> 00:04:25,279
Didn't dare join the crowd.

13
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:26,560
They wouldn't care for me anyway.

14
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,519
People at breweries usually drink a lot, don't they?

15
00:04:28,959 --> 00:04:29,519
Yeah.

16
00:04:29,839 --> 00:04:31,639
There sure are plenty of heavy drinkers here.

17
00:04:31,639 --> 00:04:32,839
But two departments can't drink.

18
00:04:33,279 --> 00:04:34,240
One is Quality Inspection.

19
00:04:34,240 --> 00:04:35,079
Sister Xuemei's department.

20
00:04:35,360 --> 00:04:36,959
The other is us drivers.

21
00:04:37,199 --> 00:04:37,759
We can't drink.

22
00:04:38,160 --> 00:04:39,600
Don't you drive a forklift?

23
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:40,480
Well...

24
00:04:40,959 --> 00:04:42,199
A forklift is still a vehicle.

25
00:04:42,399 --> 00:04:44,120
A forklift driver is still a driver.

26
00:04:44,439 --> 00:04:45,000
Drivers don't drink.

27
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:45,720
That keeps us out of trouble.

28
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:46,360
Right?

29
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,279
Right, right, right.

30
00:04:51,319 --> 00:04:52,160
Hey, Reporter Shen...

31
00:04:52,199 --> 00:04:53,519
Could you, uh, turn this off first?

32
00:04:53,839 --> 00:04:54,439
Turn it off for a second.

33
00:04:54,639 --> 00:04:55,319
Saves battery, saves battery.

34
00:04:55,319 --> 00:04:56,160
I—I want to tell you something.

35
00:04:56,319 --> 00:04:56,920
Listen...

36
00:04:57,680 --> 00:04:58,120
Well...

37
00:04:58,480 --> 00:04:59,000
It's just...

38
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,120
There's one thing I just don't get.

39
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:03,480
Why interview me?

40
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,680
I mean, all those model workers,

41
00:05:05,759 --> 00:05:06,959
and big shots in our plant, there are so many.

42
00:05:07,199 --> 00:05:08,199
Tons of them are way better than me.

43
00:05:08,199 --> 00:05:09,240
I'm nothing special.

44
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,040
You're quite special.

45
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:13,759
You just haven't realized it.

46
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:14,800
Me?

47
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:16,279
Besides eating a lot,

48
00:05:16,279 --> 00:05:17,319
I don't have anything special about me.

49
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,000
When I filmed your plant meeting,

50
00:05:20,199 --> 00:05:22,120
you were the only one writing in a notebook.

51
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,319
Oh, I see.

52
00:05:27,279 --> 00:05:28,079
I'll keep filming, then.

53
00:05:28,639 --> 00:05:29,360
Go ahead, shoot away.

54
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:30,639
Um, should I climb back up?

55
00:05:30,920 --> 00:05:31,279
Go ahead.

56
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:32,600
All right.

57
00:05:40,120 --> 00:05:40,600
Looking good.

58
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:41,959
Yeah!

59
00:05:55,120 --> 00:05:55,879
Hello?

60
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:57,480
The money's ready.

61
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:58,439
Cash.

62
00:05:58,759 --> 00:06:00,639
Under the Qianjin Road overpass,

63
00:06:00,800 --> 00:06:01,639
100 meters north.

64
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:02,920
Two o'clock.

65
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:05,160
Don't be late.

66
00:06:05,639 --> 00:06:06,279
Got it.

67
00:08:20,519 --> 00:08:21,120
Where's my money?

68
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,679
My name is Cheng Youtian.

69
00:08:36,519 --> 00:08:38,000
Head of the bottling workshop.

70
00:08:38,159 --> 00:08:38,759
Cheng Youtian.

71
00:08:39,240 --> 00:08:40,840
I've worked here for 25 years.

72
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,519
Lacheng Beer is my home,

73
00:08:44,039 --> 00:08:45,639
and everyone loves it.

74
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:46,919
How's that?

75
00:08:47,360 --> 00:08:48,120
That was great.

76
00:08:48,759 --> 00:08:49,759
Say a bit more.

77
00:08:50,720 --> 00:08:52,080
What else would you like to say?

78
00:08:54,799 --> 00:08:55,919
These rascals...

79
00:08:56,240 --> 00:08:57,279
are all like sons to me.

80
00:08:57,960 --> 00:08:58,679
They say

81
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,960
they'll take care of me when I'm old.

82
00:09:01,639 --> 00:09:02,879
Like hell I believe that!

83
00:09:03,799 --> 00:09:04,639
Can I say that?

84
00:09:04,879 --> 00:09:05,440
Sure, sure.

85
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:06,720
Say whatever you want.

86
00:09:08,120 --> 00:09:08,480
Come on, come on.

87
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:09,039
Tieping.

88
00:09:09,279 --> 00:09:09,840
Master, I...

89
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,440
I don't care.

90
00:09:10,559 --> 00:09:11,320
Be good, come here.

91
00:09:14,879 --> 00:09:15,519
Speak louder.

92
00:09:16,039 --> 00:09:16,480
It's fine.

93
00:09:21,600 --> 00:09:22,799
I'm too shy.

94
00:09:22,960 --> 00:09:23,679
Let the leadership speak.

95
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,639
In the vibrant pulse of the city,

96
00:09:31,919 --> 00:09:33,919
Lacheng Brewery stands quietly,

97
00:09:34,200 --> 00:09:37,080
like a temple brewing dreams and passion.

98
00:09:37,279 --> 00:09:38,440
Director Ma Guowen,

99
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:39,759
a leader who has dedicated many years

100
00:09:39,759 --> 00:09:41,240
to the beer industry,

101
00:09:41,240 --> 00:09:43,840
with his vision and bold decisions,

102
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,159
has guided the path for Lacheng Brewery.

103
00:09:46,159 --> 00:09:48,480
He knows quality is the company's lifeline.

104
00:09:48,679 --> 00:09:50,279
Every market insight,

105
00:09:50,279 --> 00:09:51,840
every strategic plan,

106
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:54,799
is filled with boundless passion for beer.

107
00:09:55,399 --> 00:09:57,200
Chief Engineer Chen Qingchun,

108
00:09:57,200 --> 00:09:59,519
with over 30 years of frontline experience,

109
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:01,240
holds his craft to the highest standards,

110
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,759
constantly striving for perfection.

111
00:10:09,919 --> 00:10:10,840
Chen Qingchun.

112
00:10:11,840 --> 00:10:12,919
That Ma Guowen...

113
00:10:13,360 --> 00:10:14,039
came to see me.

114
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:17,240
He wants me to join him.

115
00:10:18,399 --> 00:10:19,320
He even told me

116
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,559
that auctioning off the brewery

117
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:23,720
takes two million.

118
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:24,840
Once he flips it,

119
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,039
he'll get it right back.

120
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:28,159
Think about it.

121
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,240
Two million!

122
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:31,440
Where is he getting that money?

123
00:10:31,720 --> 00:10:32,200
You tell me.

124
00:10:32,879 --> 00:10:33,519
Right, right, right.

125
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:37,559
Isn't he pooling money?

126
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,440
So that's why I say,

127
00:10:39,919 --> 00:10:41,440
we need to pool our money too!

128
00:10:41,759 --> 00:10:42,440
Right, right!

129
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:43,000
Right!

130
00:10:43,960 --> 00:10:46,000
If we can just raise a quarter of it,

131
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:47,519
500,000,

132
00:10:48,360 --> 00:10:50,879
we'll have an entry ticket to the auction!

133
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:53,759
There are dozens,

134
00:10:54,320 --> 00:10:55,080
hundreds

135
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,279
of brothers and sisters among us.

136
00:10:57,919 --> 00:10:59,600
If we all pull together,

137
00:10:59,840 --> 00:11:01,720
we'll have the capital

138
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:04,240
to fight Ma Guowen to the death!

139
00:11:06,039 --> 00:11:06,440
Now,

140
00:11:08,559 --> 00:11:09,639
here's my pledge today:

141
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:11,840
50,000.

142
00:11:35,559 --> 00:11:36,480
If you ask me,

143
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:39,080
Lao Chen has a point.

144
00:11:40,240 --> 00:11:41,039
Either way,

145
00:11:41,399 --> 00:11:43,240
lately, whenever I think about the factory

146
00:11:43,759 --> 00:11:44,919
being ours from now on,

147
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,240
I get so excited.

148
00:12:00,159 --> 00:12:00,679
Anyone else?

149
00:12:08,679 --> 00:12:09,320
Holy smokes!

150
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,159
Look at him go!

151
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:12,080
Anyone else?

152
00:12:13,039 --> 00:12:13,639
Um...

153
00:12:14,039 --> 00:12:15,840
I only have 500 on me today.

154
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,120
I'll put in this much for now.

155
00:12:17,639 --> 00:12:18,360
As for the rest...

156
00:12:18,399 --> 00:12:19,360
I'll go back and fetch it for you.

157
00:12:20,799 --> 00:12:21,639
You gotta admit...

158
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:24,720
Cao Jun's attitude is exactly what we need.

159
00:12:25,039 --> 00:12:26,360
Come on, write him down.

160
00:12:26,559 --> 00:12:27,039
500.

161
00:12:27,320 --> 00:12:28,120
Put down 500 for now.

162
00:12:28,320 --> 00:12:28,840
Okay.

163
00:12:29,039 --> 00:12:29,480
Right, right.

164
00:12:29,559 --> 00:12:30,279
Write it down for him.

165
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,200
I've got 100 here.

166
00:12:31,919 --> 00:12:32,720
Put me down first.

167
00:12:37,159 --> 00:12:37,840
I've got some too.

168
00:12:39,759 --> 00:12:40,519
Chunyan, write it down.

169
00:12:40,519 --> 00:12:41,120
Here's mine.

170
00:12:41,120 --> 00:12:41,960
Got 400 here.

171
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:43,080
Wait, hold on.

172
00:12:43,080 --> 00:12:43,559
Write it down in a second.

173
00:12:43,639 --> 00:12:44,320
Chuan, Chuan!

174
00:12:44,320 --> 00:12:44,919
Lend me 200.

175
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:46,480
How much?

176
00:12:46,840 --> 00:12:47,519
200. Put me down for it!

177
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,039
200.

178
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:48,559
Wait!

179
00:12:49,320 --> 00:12:50,440
Lend me 100 too!

180
00:12:52,200 --> 00:12:52,960
125.

181
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,159
One... 100.

182
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:56,519
From me and Tieping.

183
00:12:57,440 --> 00:12:57,919
Chunyan!

184
00:12:58,120 --> 00:12:59,080
Me too, Chunyan!

185
00:12:59,200 --> 00:12:59,720
Tieping.

186
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:00,600
110.

187
00:13:00,679 --> 00:13:01,159
Ge Shun.

188
00:13:01,159 --> 00:13:01,919
Ge Shun, 100.

189
00:13:01,919 --> 00:13:02,600
Slow down, everyone.

190
00:13:02,639 --> 00:13:03,240
Slow down, slow down.

191
00:13:03,320 --> 00:13:04,000
One at a time!

192
00:13:04,159 --> 00:13:04,480
Take it easy.

193
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:05,000
Take it easy, I'll go get the rest!

194
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:05,840
One at a time!

195
00:13:06,519 --> 00:13:07,080
Here, here...

196
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:07,840
What's this?

197
00:13:08,559 --> 00:13:08,919
Hold on.

198
00:13:09,200 --> 00:13:09,720
Don't be so stingy.

199
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:10,840
Okay, I've got you all down.

200
00:13:11,159 --> 00:13:12,440
Add two more yuan for Shunzi.

201
00:13:12,559 --> 00:13:13,559
Here's ten yuan.

202
00:13:13,840 --> 00:13:14,840
Here, here, here.

203
00:13:15,039 --> 00:13:15,519
Sun Jianguo, seven yuan. Let's just...

204
00:13:15,519 --> 00:13:16,480
Just call it 15.

205
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:17,639
The amount doesn't matter.

206
00:13:17,679 --> 00:13:18,480
It's the thought that counts.

207
00:13:20,639 --> 00:13:21,399
Shunzi, nine yuan.

208
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:21,919
Seven yuan.

209
00:13:21,919 --> 00:13:22,480
I'll add one yuan.

210
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
Who pitches in seven yuan?

211
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:24,600
Nine yuan.

212
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,600
Come on, come on.

213
00:13:26,679 --> 00:13:27,000
Come on, now.

214
00:13:27,039 --> 00:13:27,559
Here, here, here.

215
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:28,879
Don't crowd!

216
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:29,519
Listen to Chunyan!

217
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,320
Alright, anyone else?

218
00:13:31,519 --> 00:13:32,000
Anyone else?

219
00:13:34,799 --> 00:13:35,200
Yeah!

220
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:36,320
Yeah, yeah!

221
00:14:09,840 --> 00:14:10,679
At 7:30 this morning,

222
00:14:11,039 --> 00:14:12,679
a worker from Lacheng Brewery called it in.

223
00:14:12,960 --> 00:14:14,519
He said this three-wheeler belongs to Cao Jun.

224
00:14:14,840 --> 00:14:15,679
Preliminary examination shows

225
00:14:15,799 --> 00:14:17,399
the victim died of asphyxiation.

226
00:14:17,840 --> 00:14:18,799
Time of death

227
00:14:18,799 --> 00:14:20,080
was between 2:00 and 2:30 a.m.

228
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:20,840
No injuries on this side, right?

229
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:23,120
Multiple strike marks on the head,

230
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:24,960
likely caused by a blunt object.

231
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:26,399
There are ligature marks on the neck as well.

232
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,559
The killer is most likely male.

233
00:14:29,120 --> 00:14:29,759
Done.

234
00:14:29,759 --> 00:14:30,879
Bottle caps again.

235
00:14:31,799 --> 00:14:32,600
And a black plastic bag.

236
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:35,000
Cao Jun...

237
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,080
We just questioned him,

238
00:14:37,080 --> 00:14:38,480
and now he's been murdered.

239
00:14:40,919 --> 00:14:42,320
Talk about brazen.

240
00:14:42,919 --> 00:14:43,480
Captain Han,

241
00:14:43,840 --> 00:14:45,919
can we strongly suspect

242
00:14:46,080 --> 00:14:47,000
a serial killer?

243
00:14:48,279 --> 00:14:49,440
They're taunting us.

244
00:14:51,519 --> 00:14:53,639
Pull all of Cao Jun's call logs.

245
00:14:53,759 --> 00:14:55,200
Especially right before he died.

246
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:56,679
Yes, sir.

247
00:14:58,960 --> 00:14:59,639
Where's Gao Xuelin?

248
00:15:00,240 --> 00:15:01,879
He went to the old factory area.

249
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:53,440
Pull over!

250
00:15:54,240 --> 00:15:54,799
Stop, stop, stop!

251
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:55,960
What's your business?

252
00:15:56,360 --> 00:15:57,159
Park by the curb.

253
00:15:57,279 --> 00:15:58,080
Get out and sign in.

254
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,200
I'm heading to Workshop One.

255
00:15:59,360 --> 00:16:01,159
Whichever workshop it is, you gotta sign in.

256
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,159
What's his problem?

257
00:16:02,279 --> 00:16:03,240
Cocky bastard.

258
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:04,559
Get out and sign in.

259
00:16:06,039 --> 00:16:06,679
Who knows?

260
00:16:06,720 --> 00:16:07,360
Giving me attitude.

261
00:16:07,399 --> 00:16:07,759
Where's he from?

262
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:08,679
Workshop One, my ass.

263
00:16:08,679 --> 00:16:09,440
Never seen him before.

264
00:16:10,159 --> 00:16:11,080
Lacheng Criminal Police.

265
00:16:11,559 --> 00:16:11,960
Holy crap!

266
00:16:12,320 --> 00:16:13,320
Even the detectives are here.

267
00:16:13,720 --> 00:16:15,039
What happened to our plant?

268
00:16:15,679 --> 00:16:16,360
This... this...

269
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,279
Someone hit the statue.

270
00:16:17,279 --> 00:16:18,840
And Cao Jun was strangled to death.

271
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,440
The statue got smashed.

272
00:16:20,879 --> 00:16:21,759
It got rammed right here.

273
00:16:21,759 --> 00:16:22,200
Look.

274
00:16:22,200 --> 00:16:22,960
Take a look here.

275
00:16:23,399 --> 00:16:24,200
Who hit the statue?

276
00:16:25,279 --> 00:16:26,399
Our plant's former chief engineer.

277
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,399
Name's Chen Qingchun.

278
00:16:27,519 --> 00:16:28,279
He came by early this morning...

279
00:16:28,399 --> 00:16:28,960
...saying he hit it.

280
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:29,960
Then Traffic Police took him away.

281
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:31,799
When was it hit?

282
00:16:32,120 --> 00:16:32,639
Last night.

283
00:16:32,919 --> 00:16:33,320
In the middle of the night.

284
00:16:33,799 --> 00:16:35,519
I was fast asleep, having a sweet dream.

285
00:16:35,639 --> 00:16:36,480
Then BAM!

286
00:16:36,600 --> 00:16:37,799
I thought someone crashed into my bed.

287
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:38,679
Captain Han.

288
00:16:39,919 --> 00:16:42,159
Wasn't midnight Cao Jun's time of death?

289
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:46,480
Did he hit it on purpose,

290
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:47,200
or was it an accident?

291
00:16:47,679 --> 00:16:48,519
How would I know?

292
00:16:48,519 --> 00:16:49,240
I'm just a security guard.

293
00:16:49,279 --> 00:16:50,399
That's not my call.

294
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:51,559
That's for the traffic cops.

295
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:52,799
Were you on duty last night?

296
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:53,600
Yes, I was.

297
00:16:55,600 --> 00:16:56,559
Can I drive the car in?

298
00:16:56,759 --> 00:16:57,240
Sure, sure.

299
00:16:57,240 --> 00:16:57,799
Yeah, you can.

300
00:16:57,840 --> 00:16:58,679
I... I can drive it for you.

301
00:16:58,759 --> 00:16:59,200
No need.

302
00:16:59,799 --> 00:17:00,279
Don't trust me?

303
00:17:00,759 --> 00:17:02,320
Cut the crap.

304
00:17:02,679 --> 00:17:03,440
I'm actually a decent driver.

305
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:04,599
How do I get to Workshop One?

306
00:17:05,759 --> 00:17:06,880
Go inside, head in and take a left.

307
00:17:07,279 --> 00:17:07,559
Okay.

308
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:08,759
Take... take it slow!

309
00:17:09,079 --> 00:17:10,039
Hey, hey!

310
00:17:10,160 --> 00:17:11,119
A gray Jetta!

311
00:17:11,119 --> 00:17:11,880
Letting one in!

312
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,559
What are you doing taking a stroll here?

313
00:17:18,799 --> 00:17:19,359
A stroll?

314
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,200
Someone just died around here.

315
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:22,839
Who'd come here for a stroll?

316
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:25,359
Good that you know.

317
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:27,119
Don't get in the way of official business.

318
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:28,519
Who are you kidding?

319
00:17:28,759 --> 00:17:29,799
Official business?

320
00:17:30,039 --> 00:17:31,440
You wouldn't be all by yourself.

321
00:17:32,079 --> 00:17:33,359
My partner's right nearby.

322
00:17:35,119 --> 00:17:36,519
The one stalking me these past few days...

323
00:17:36,839 --> 00:17:37,920
It wasn't you, was it?

324
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,720
I'm not a creep.

325
00:17:40,200 --> 00:17:41,079
Why would I stalk you?

326
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:50,920
I was wondering why you picked this spot.

327
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,920
There isn't even a camera around.

328
00:17:54,960 --> 00:17:56,200
You don't look that old,

329
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:58,279
but you're quite calculating.

330
00:17:59,599 --> 00:18:00,279
Coincidence.

331
00:18:01,359 --> 00:18:02,039
Just a coincidence.

332
00:18:05,920 --> 00:18:07,759
Since we ran into each other,

333
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:08,839
let's chat.

334
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,680
Tell me old stories about Lacheng Brewery.

335
00:18:12,240 --> 00:18:13,359
There are plenty of old stories.

336
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,400
Which part do you want to hear, Officer Gao?

337
00:18:16,720 --> 00:18:17,519
Liu Xuemei.

338
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:24,559
Yesterday,

339
00:18:24,759 --> 00:18:26,559
I watched your "Malt Kingdom" a few times.

340
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:27,559
It was good.

341
00:18:29,079 --> 00:18:30,200
But I have a question

342
00:18:31,039 --> 00:18:32,319
for Director Shen.

343
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,240
Back when you were filming,

344
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:37,960
there was a beer taster named Liu Xuemei

345
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:38,920
who froze to death.

346
00:18:39,599 --> 00:18:40,680
On Millennium Eve.

347
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:43,400
It was big news in Lacheng back then.

348
00:18:43,720 --> 00:18:44,799
It was even on TV.

349
00:18:46,319 --> 00:18:47,799
You were the one who interviewed her, right?

350
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,279
Yet I

351
00:18:49,640 --> 00:18:51,400
didn't see her in "Malt Kingdom."

352
00:18:51,960 --> 00:18:52,880
Not a single mention,

353
00:18:53,039 --> 00:18:54,279
not even a single shot.

354
00:18:54,559 --> 00:18:55,000
Why?

355
00:18:55,839 --> 00:18:57,480
There were lots of people at the brewery.

356
00:18:58,079 --> 00:18:59,319
Not everyone

357
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:00,920
made it into the documentary.

358
00:19:02,359 --> 00:19:03,480
Did you interview her, then?

359
00:19:04,200 --> 00:19:05,000
I did.

360
00:19:05,359 --> 00:19:06,400
Then why wasn't she in it?

361
00:19:06,759 --> 00:19:07,640
Didn't I just tell you?

362
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:08,519
There were lots of people.

363
00:19:08,519 --> 00:19:09,720
Not everyone was included.

364
00:19:11,640 --> 00:19:13,680
You were there the day Ma Guowen bid on the plant, right?

365
00:19:14,359 --> 00:19:15,160
Was Liu Xuemei there?

366
00:19:15,759 --> 00:19:16,799
Did anything happen?

367
00:19:19,039 --> 00:19:20,000
No comment.

368
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:23,039
Your documentary

369
00:19:23,039 --> 00:19:25,000
hid a lot of the truth back then.

370
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:26,839
How did Qian Yichuan's leg get crippled?

371
00:19:27,319 --> 00:19:29,799
Cheng Youtian, Tu Chunyan, Cao Jun,

372
00:19:30,720 --> 00:19:31,480
Zhao Haipeng...

373
00:19:31,759 --> 00:19:32,960
How did they all end up laid off?

374
00:19:33,599 --> 00:19:35,160
Was it because they wanted to bid on the plant

375
00:19:35,160 --> 00:19:36,160
and crossed Ma Guowen?

376
00:19:36,400 --> 00:19:37,279
Liu Xuemei's death...

377
00:19:37,279 --> 00:19:38,400
did it have anything to do with this?

378
00:19:45,799 --> 00:19:47,359
I'd like to ask you something too, Officer Gao.

379
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:49,960
What is Liu Xuemei to you?

380
00:19:50,359 --> 00:19:51,720
Why do you care so much about her?

381
00:19:52,880 --> 00:19:53,920
I know she had a son.

382
00:19:54,319 --> 00:19:55,359
He was seven or eight back then,

383
00:19:56,039 --> 00:19:57,359
around your age.

384
00:20:09,640 --> 00:20:10,400
Not answering

385
00:20:10,960 --> 00:20:11,640
means you're admitting it.

386
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:15,200
What you just said

387
00:20:15,559 --> 00:20:17,319
doesn't sound like recent findings.

388
00:20:18,039 --> 00:20:20,920
It sounds more like

389
00:20:21,160 --> 00:20:23,039
you started watching these people long ago.

390
00:20:23,880 --> 00:20:25,319
I don't need to tell you my business.

391
00:20:26,480 --> 00:20:28,359
Answer my question directly.

392
00:20:29,319 --> 00:20:30,759
Why should I answer you?

393
00:20:31,359 --> 00:20:32,559
Am I a suspect?

394
00:20:33,599 --> 00:20:35,480
You haven't solved Ma Guowen's death,

395
00:20:35,880 --> 00:20:37,119
and now you're grilling me about Liu Xuemei.

396
00:20:37,720 --> 00:20:38,960
Go do your actual job.

397
00:20:40,039 --> 00:20:40,680
Stop right there.

398
00:20:42,440 --> 00:20:44,319
What really happened the day Liu Xuemei died?

399
00:20:44,319 --> 00:20:45,519
You definitely shot footage.

400
00:20:46,039 --> 00:20:46,880
Give me the footage.

401
00:20:47,440 --> 00:20:48,480
I don't have it.

402
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:50,400
You just said you interviewed her.

403
00:20:51,039 --> 00:20:52,200
Where's the unused footage from back then?

404
00:20:52,880 --> 00:20:53,799
Why are you afraid to show it?

405
00:20:54,759 --> 00:20:55,799
You've crossed the line.

406
00:21:08,839 --> 00:21:10,079
Who are you really?

407
00:21:11,759 --> 00:21:13,599
What's your connection to Liu Xuemei?

408
00:21:15,119 --> 00:21:17,079
You don't care about what you should be investigating,

409
00:21:17,519 --> 00:21:19,200
yet you won't leave Liu Xuemei alone.

410
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,880
I should be asking you,

411
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,519
what's your deal?

412
00:21:53,319 --> 00:21:54,319
Go call him over for me.

413
00:21:54,599 --> 00:21:55,119
Sure.

414
00:21:55,119 --> 00:21:55,799
Thanks.

415
00:22:08,039 --> 00:22:09,359
You're Liu Tieping, right?

416
00:22:10,319 --> 00:22:12,200
We're from the Lacheng Criminal Investigation Detachment.

417
00:22:12,799 --> 00:22:13,920
Since you reported the crime,

418
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:15,480
I need to ask you a few questions.

419
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:16,799
This is Officer Han Chuang.

420
00:22:17,279 --> 00:22:17,880
Hello.

421
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:20,440
You're pretty dedicated to your job.

422
00:22:21,319 --> 00:22:22,000
The factory director is dead,

423
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:23,000
the plant is being sold off,

424
00:22:23,119 --> 00:22:24,839
and a lot of workers stopped showing up.

425
00:22:25,359 --> 00:22:26,680
Yet you're still here working.

426
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:30,960
So,

427
00:22:31,440 --> 00:22:32,920
let me ask you a few things.

428
00:22:34,640 --> 00:22:37,119
The plant is over ten kilometers from the scene.

429
00:22:37,119 --> 00:22:39,200
How did you find Cao Jun's body?

430
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,920
I passed by on my way to work.

431
00:22:42,799 --> 00:22:43,720
Where do you live?

432
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:45,599
The west tenement building.

433
00:22:46,799 --> 00:22:48,160
The west tenement building.

434
00:22:50,480 --> 00:22:52,880
What were you doing last night after ten?

435
00:22:55,559 --> 00:22:56,400
I was drinking.

436
00:22:57,279 --> 00:22:58,359
Where were you drinking?

437
00:23:00,960 --> 00:23:01,960
Just in my dorm.

438
00:23:03,440 --> 00:23:04,440
Who were you drinking with?

439
00:23:06,799 --> 00:23:07,359
Li San.

440
00:23:08,920 --> 00:23:09,680
That's him right there.

441
00:23:11,559 --> 00:23:12,319
Go over and ask him.

442
00:23:16,319 --> 00:23:18,319
How late were you drinking last night?

443
00:23:22,079 --> 00:23:22,680
Don't know.

444
00:23:24,240 --> 00:23:25,319
Then how much did you drink?

445
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:36,960
I don't know.

446
00:23:39,079 --> 00:23:40,160
What time did you wake up?

447
00:23:42,160 --> 00:23:44,160
I... I went to work as soon as I woke up.

448
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,839
Then how did you find Cao Jun's body this morning?

449
00:23:50,319 --> 00:23:51,559
I just passed by on my way to work.

450
00:23:54,440 --> 00:23:55,119
And then?

451
00:23:58,480 --> 00:23:58,839
I... I...

452
00:23:58,839 --> 00:24:01,160
Mostly, I just noticed his car.

453
00:24:01,839 --> 00:24:03,440
You recognize Cao Jun's car, right?

454
00:24:04,440 --> 00:24:05,599
You recognized that car.

455
00:24:11,240 --> 00:24:12,480
Think back.

456
00:24:13,279 --> 00:24:15,759
Who in the factory had bad blood

457
00:24:15,960 --> 00:24:17,319
with Ma Guowen and Cao Jun?

458
00:24:24,759 --> 00:24:26,960
How many years have you known Ma Guowen and Cao Jun?

459
00:24:30,799 --> 00:24:32,839
They were already there when I joined the factory.

460
00:24:35,799 --> 00:24:37,279
How many years have you been at the factory?

461
00:24:39,799 --> 00:24:40,839
Around ten years, I guess.

462
00:24:44,279 --> 00:24:45,519
Then think about it.

463
00:24:45,839 --> 00:24:47,680
Normally, who was

464
00:24:47,920 --> 00:24:49,400
on good terms with Ma Guowen?

465
00:25:04,200 --> 00:25:05,720
Who was close to Cao Jun?

466
00:25:12,839 --> 00:25:13,759
Haven't sobered up yet?

467
00:25:15,519 --> 00:25:16,240
I'm sober.

468
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:17,319
I'm working.

469
00:25:19,559 --> 00:25:20,119
All right.

470
00:25:20,559 --> 00:25:21,079
Look.

471
00:25:22,279 --> 00:25:23,640
I'll give you my number.

472
00:25:24,680 --> 00:25:25,440
Here's my number.

473
00:25:25,519 --> 00:25:26,240
My name's Han.

474
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:28,799
When your head clears up,

475
00:25:28,799 --> 00:25:29,680
if you remember anything,

476
00:25:29,720 --> 00:25:30,559
give me a call.

477
00:25:30,599 --> 00:25:31,200
Okay?

478
00:25:34,039 --> 00:25:34,799
Drink less.

479
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:36,000
It rots your brain.

480
00:25:41,400 --> 00:25:42,160
Tech investigated.

481
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:44,400
The last call made to Cao Jun

482
00:25:44,400 --> 00:25:45,359
was from an unregistered SIM card.

483
00:25:45,839 --> 00:25:47,319
So that lead is dead.

484
00:25:47,759 --> 00:25:48,119
Right.

485
00:25:48,559 --> 00:25:49,400
Cao Jun died last night

486
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:51,319
between two and two-thirty, right?

487
00:25:51,640 --> 00:25:52,119
That guy? Yeah.

488
00:25:52,119 --> 00:25:54,160
The body was found this morning.

489
00:25:54,440 --> 00:25:56,160
Last night at ten,

490
00:25:56,759 --> 00:25:58,839
he was drinking with friends until two.

491
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:00,759
What time was the statue at the gate hit?

492
00:26:00,960 --> 00:26:02,640
A little after two in the morning.

493
00:26:04,519 --> 00:26:05,680
The crime scene

494
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:07,440
is over ten kilometers from the factory.

495
00:26:08,519 --> 00:26:10,079
It couldn't be Chen Qingchun either.

496
00:26:10,319 --> 00:26:11,119
It's too far.

497
00:26:11,400 --> 00:26:11,920
Impossible.

498
00:26:12,960 --> 00:26:14,599
Your mind sure works fast.

499
00:26:15,039 --> 00:26:16,599
Jumping all over the place.

500
00:26:16,799 --> 00:26:17,640
Is Gao back yet?

501
00:26:18,119 --> 00:26:19,319
I've been busy all morning.

502
00:26:19,400 --> 00:26:20,640
Who's got time to check on him?

503
00:26:24,920 --> 00:26:25,279
Over here.

504
00:26:25,359 --> 00:26:25,960
Cai.

505
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:28,480
You're up so early.

506
00:26:28,519 --> 00:26:29,279
What are you having?

507
00:26:30,039 --> 00:26:30,759
Boss,

508
00:26:31,640 --> 00:26:32,480
a bowl of beef noodles.

509
00:26:32,640 --> 00:26:33,400
Sure thing, just a moment.

510
00:26:34,000 --> 00:26:35,720
I thought people in our line of work were night owls

511
00:26:35,720 --> 00:26:36,640
who slept in.

512
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:39,519
How did that inquiry go?

513
00:26:39,839 --> 00:26:41,319
I was just about to report to you.

514
00:26:41,839 --> 00:26:42,440
Let me tell you,

515
00:26:42,440 --> 00:26:43,119
it's such a coincidence.

516
00:26:43,599 --> 00:26:44,440
He's from Qingzhou.

517
00:26:44,680 --> 00:26:45,599
I'm from Qingzhou too.

518
00:26:45,759 --> 00:26:47,200
And we went to the same middle school.

519
00:26:47,440 --> 00:26:48,279
He was two grades below me,

520
00:26:48,279 --> 00:26:49,039
so I didn't know him.

521
00:26:49,759 --> 00:26:51,759
But I know some of his classmates.

522
00:26:52,079 --> 00:26:53,119
So where he lives,

523
00:26:53,119 --> 00:26:54,000
who he's closest to...

524
00:26:54,079 --> 00:26:55,039
I found it all out.

525
00:26:56,160 --> 00:26:57,759
I'll send the info to your phone.

526
00:26:57,799 --> 00:26:58,319
Okay.

527
00:27:02,160 --> 00:27:02,759
Chuang!

528
00:27:03,119 --> 00:27:03,640
Cai!

529
00:27:04,160 --> 00:27:05,319
I'm done checking the old factory area.

530
00:27:05,799 --> 00:27:07,400
Brought you guys some breakfast too.

531
00:27:07,640 --> 00:27:08,359
The steamed buns are still piping hot.

532
00:27:08,359 --> 00:27:08,920
Have some.

533
00:27:08,920 --> 00:27:09,559
Look what time it is.

534
00:27:09,559 --> 00:27:10,599
Breakfast now?

535
00:27:26,160 --> 00:27:26,720
So what?

536
00:27:28,359 --> 00:27:29,039
How many beers I drink,

537
00:27:29,039 --> 00:27:29,920
am I supposed to count?

538
00:27:30,799 --> 00:27:31,640
I smoke too.

539
00:27:32,799 --> 00:27:34,119
How many cigarettes I smoke a day,

540
00:27:34,799 --> 00:27:35,599
how would I remember?

541
00:27:36,839 --> 00:27:39,279
What time did you last see Cao Jun last night?

542
00:27:41,359 --> 00:27:41,960
Past eight, I guess.

543
00:27:42,640 --> 00:27:43,519
Where did you see him?

544
00:27:44,319 --> 00:27:45,400
Downstairs by the trash.

545
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:46,799
Did you say anything to each other?

546
00:27:49,759 --> 00:27:50,680
Didn't say a thing.

547
00:27:52,799 --> 00:27:54,000
Are you and Cao Jun close?

548
00:27:56,200 --> 00:27:56,720
Not close.

549
00:27:58,119 --> 00:27:58,799
Not close?

550
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,720
Weren't you coworkers at the old Lacheng Brewery?

551
00:28:02,480 --> 00:28:03,480
How could you not be close?

552
00:28:08,200 --> 00:28:09,559
Our entire building

553
00:28:09,720 --> 00:28:11,079
worked at the old Lacheng Brewery.

554
00:28:11,720 --> 00:28:12,680
That's dozens of families.

555
00:28:13,680 --> 00:28:14,880
Am I supposed to know everyone?

556
00:28:16,200 --> 00:28:17,000
Think about it.

557
00:28:18,319 --> 00:28:19,319
Out of dozens of families,

558
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:21,440
why did I single you out?

559
00:28:26,319 --> 00:28:27,240
I have no idea.

560
00:28:30,400 --> 00:28:31,480
Let me give you a hint.

561
00:28:33,039 --> 00:28:34,599
Someone said at eight last night,

562
00:28:34,640 --> 00:28:35,519
you went to Cao Jun's place.

563
00:28:35,559 --> 00:28:36,279
Is that true or not?

564
00:28:36,759 --> 00:28:37,480
Who said that?

565
00:28:37,759 --> 00:28:38,680
Never mind who.

566
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,400
Did you go?

567
00:28:39,400 --> 00:28:40,079
Is it true?

568
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:42,400
Was it Shen Leshui?

569
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:48,880
I've got beef with her.

570
00:28:49,400 --> 00:28:51,160
I just left some stuff by her door,

571
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:52,160
and she messes with me every day,

572
00:28:52,160 --> 00:28:53,400
snitching on me everywhere.

573
00:28:54,079 --> 00:28:54,960
That woman,

574
00:28:55,920 --> 00:28:57,359
she's just like the saying—

575
00:28:57,359 --> 00:28:58,279
nothing but a big mouth.

576
00:28:58,359 --> 00:28:59,240
You can't believe a word she says.

577
00:28:59,279 --> 00:28:59,640
That's enough.

578
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:01,640
None of this has anything to do with the case.

579
00:29:01,839 --> 00:29:02,799
What I'm asking you right now is,

580
00:29:02,839 --> 00:29:03,799
at eight last night,

581
00:29:03,880 --> 00:29:05,200
did you go to Cao Jun's place?

582
00:29:05,599 --> 00:29:06,559
Think carefully.

583
00:29:07,400 --> 00:29:07,920
This

584
00:29:07,960 --> 00:29:09,960
is vital to both the victim, Cao Jun, and you.

585
00:29:15,640 --> 00:29:16,400
I went.

586
00:29:17,240 --> 00:29:18,200
But we didn't do anything.

587
00:29:18,480 --> 00:29:19,279
Didn't do anything?

588
00:29:20,119 --> 00:29:21,359
Think carefully before you speak.

589
00:29:22,079 --> 00:29:23,000
You go to his home,

590
00:29:23,279 --> 00:29:24,039
do nothing at all—

591
00:29:24,759 --> 00:29:25,559
then what did you go for?

592
00:29:27,559 --> 00:29:28,440
He asked me over.

593
00:29:29,519 --> 00:29:30,400
To do what?

594
00:29:34,039 --> 00:29:34,720
Sleep together.

595
00:29:35,319 --> 00:29:36,640
Didn't you say you weren't close?

596
00:29:37,240 --> 00:29:38,839
You chat a bit and get close, right?

597
00:29:39,920 --> 00:29:40,759
What's the problem?

598
00:29:41,240 --> 00:29:42,160
He has no wife,

599
00:29:43,319 --> 00:29:44,200
and I have no husband.

600
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:46,920
Can't the two of us sleep together?

601
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:53,960
You can.

602
00:29:54,400 --> 00:29:55,240
I didn't say you couldn't.

603
00:29:55,799 --> 00:29:56,599
Then why ask?

604
00:29:57,400 --> 00:29:58,240
All the more reason to ask.

605
00:29:58,920 --> 00:30:00,279
What state was Cao Jun in that night?

606
00:30:01,079 --> 00:30:02,160
What do you mean, "what state"?

607
00:30:03,279 --> 00:30:04,599
You want details?

608
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,440
Fine.

609
00:30:10,920 --> 00:30:11,720
Cao Jun—

610
00:30:12,319 --> 00:30:13,200
who was he close to?

611
00:30:14,759 --> 00:30:15,359
Don't know.

612
00:30:15,920 --> 00:30:17,680
Who did Cao Jun have bad blood with?

613
00:30:20,279 --> 00:30:20,960
Don't know.

614
00:30:21,319 --> 00:30:22,720
Fine. Playing dumb on everything, huh?

615
00:30:24,119 --> 00:30:24,720
Tu Chunyan.

616
00:30:25,200 --> 00:30:25,960
Let me tell you something.

617
00:30:26,440 --> 00:30:27,839
As far as we know,

618
00:30:28,119 --> 00:30:29,880
you were the last person to see Cao Jun yesterday,

619
00:30:30,279 --> 00:30:32,000
and you two had intimate contact.

620
00:30:32,759 --> 00:30:34,359
I hope you'll cooperate,

621
00:30:34,400 --> 00:30:36,200
and tell me everything you know.

622
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:38,359
Otherwise, once you walk out that door,

623
00:30:39,079 --> 00:30:40,000
I'm going to investigate you.

624
00:30:41,079 --> 00:30:42,279
Want to make a bet?

625
00:30:42,720 --> 00:30:43,920
I can dig up every single thing

626
00:30:43,960 --> 00:30:44,839
you've ever done.

627
00:30:45,519 --> 00:30:46,640
When I haul you back in,

628
00:30:46,640 --> 00:30:47,400
things will be very different.

629
00:30:47,640 --> 00:30:48,599
Weigh your options.

630
00:31:15,079 --> 00:31:15,839
Cao Jun...

631
00:31:17,599 --> 00:31:18,960
has a habit of keeping a diary.

632
00:31:20,960 --> 00:31:22,680
There's a diary under his pillow.

633
00:31:23,279 --> 00:31:24,920
He wrote all kinds of weird things in it.

634
00:31:25,880 --> 00:31:26,759
I didn't really get it.

635
00:31:27,400 --> 00:31:28,559
If you want to know,

636
00:31:29,400 --> 00:31:30,920
go take a look at it yourself.

637
00:31:34,200 --> 00:31:34,960
What kind of notebook?

638
00:31:37,640 --> 00:31:39,240
A little red notebook.

639
00:31:40,599 --> 00:31:41,720
It has the word "Award" on it.

640
00:31:43,279 --> 00:31:44,359
Back in the day,

641
00:31:46,519 --> 00:31:48,440
the factory gave it to him for being a model worker.

642
00:31:55,000 --> 00:31:57,039
What time did you leave Cao Jun's place last night?

643
00:32:01,519 --> 00:32:02,440
Around nine or so.

644
00:32:04,680 --> 00:32:06,079
Once he fell asleep, I left.

645
00:32:10,839 --> 00:32:12,119
Was there money exchanged between you two?

646
00:32:19,559 --> 00:32:21,519
Was there money exchanged between you two?

647
00:32:22,400 --> 00:32:23,759
I don't make money that way.

648
00:32:27,880 --> 00:32:29,160
Cao Jun is a good man.

649
00:32:29,160 --> 00:32:30,079
You know that?

650
00:32:31,319 --> 00:32:32,759
I've known him for so many years,

651
00:32:33,599 --> 00:32:35,960
and he never once lost his temper at anyone.

652
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:38,319
I have no idea who he could've crossed.

653
00:32:39,599 --> 00:32:41,240
Whoever killed Cao Jun,

654
00:32:41,920 --> 00:32:43,200
they'll die a miserable death!

655
00:32:43,599 --> 00:32:44,680
You cops,

656
00:32:44,680 --> 00:32:45,640
do your damn job!

657
00:32:45,720 --> 00:32:47,440
Hurry up and catch the killer!

658
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,559
Please sit down first.

659
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:12,640
I found it.

660
00:33:12,720 --> 00:33:13,079
Chuang.

661
00:33:13,519 --> 00:33:15,079
The diary from Tu Chunyan's statement.

662
00:33:17,680 --> 00:33:19,039
"Soul Massage."

663
00:33:19,599 --> 00:33:20,079
This one.

664
00:33:21,359 --> 00:33:21,960
Xiao Wu.

665
00:33:22,519 --> 00:33:23,240
Coming, Chuang.

666
00:33:25,119 --> 00:33:25,559
Here.

667
00:33:26,200 --> 00:33:27,720
Go through all the info

668
00:33:27,799 --> 00:33:28,319
in this diary.

669
00:33:28,480 --> 00:33:28,839
Got it.

670
00:33:28,839 --> 00:33:29,319
Check it thoroughly.

671
00:33:36,319 --> 00:33:37,000
Here, give it to me.

672
00:33:41,160 --> 00:33:41,839
What does this mean?

673
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:43,480
He used to drive a forklift.

674
00:33:43,480 --> 00:33:44,279
Now he drives an auto-rickshaw.

675
00:33:44,279 --> 00:33:46,079
Why would he keep photos of scrapped cars?

676
00:33:51,319 --> 00:33:52,440
Let me see what it says.

677
00:33:55,240 --> 00:33:56,000
Touch-up paint.

678
00:33:56,720 --> 00:33:58,039
Scrapping procedure.

679
00:33:58,640 --> 00:34:01,200
Retirement age for division-level cadres.

680
00:34:06,559 --> 00:34:07,519
"I found..."

681
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:10,360
What, you think I can't read?

682
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:16,559
"I found the traitor who betrayed our fellow workers."

683
00:34:17,119 --> 00:34:18,800
"With leverage on him, I can turn things around."

684
00:34:20,079 --> 00:34:20,599
Traitor.

685
00:34:23,519 --> 00:34:25,159
Chuang, I think there's something off with that car.

686
00:34:25,559 --> 00:34:26,000
Xiao Wu.

687
00:34:26,800 --> 00:34:27,480
In Lacheng,

688
00:34:27,480 --> 00:34:28,960
isn't there a car scrapyard?

689
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:29,840
Yeah.

690
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:31,280
I know it.

691
00:34:31,800 --> 00:34:32,840
The biggest one is called

692
00:34:33,079 --> 00:34:33,679
Xinbin.

693
00:34:34,000 --> 00:34:34,719
Contact them right away,

694
00:34:34,719 --> 00:34:35,719
then send me the address.

695
00:34:35,920 --> 00:34:36,599
We'll head over soon.

696
00:34:38,880 --> 00:34:39,519
Hurry up.

697
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:43,719
Go on.

698
00:34:50,800 --> 00:34:51,360
Chuang.

699
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:53,840
Don't be mad anymore.

700
00:34:55,239 --> 00:34:55,960
I know I screwed up.

701
00:34:59,840 --> 00:35:00,360
Look,

702
00:35:00,360 --> 00:35:01,960
what did I tell you the other day?

703
00:35:03,039 --> 00:35:04,320
I was just so anxious.

704
00:35:08,119 --> 00:35:08,679
All right.

705
00:35:10,119 --> 00:35:10,960
Your punishment:

706
00:35:11,400 --> 00:35:12,239
buy steamed buns for three days.

707
00:35:12,400 --> 00:35:13,119
Hear me?

708
00:35:13,920 --> 00:35:15,280
I can buy them for ten days!

709
00:35:15,599 --> 00:35:16,719
I'll get you different kinds every day.

710
00:35:18,519 --> 00:35:19,039
Keep looking into it.

711
00:35:19,400 --> 00:35:19,800
Got it.

712
00:35:28,519 --> 00:35:30,079
How long have you run this scrapyard?

713
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:31,639
Quite a while now.

714
00:35:33,119 --> 00:35:35,079
When was the last time you saw Cao Jun?

715
00:35:35,800 --> 00:35:36,800
Last week.

716
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:37,719
On the 28th.

717
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:40,679
You remember that pretty clearly.

718
00:35:41,920 --> 00:35:43,280
It was my birthday.

719
00:35:43,679 --> 00:35:44,920
We had a few drinks together.

720
00:35:45,079 --> 00:35:46,559
Who knew something would happen to him a few days later?

721
00:35:47,920 --> 00:35:48,559
Brothers?

722
00:35:48,800 --> 00:35:49,320
What kind of brothers?

723
00:35:49,360 --> 00:35:50,400
Are you full brothers?

724
00:35:51,280 --> 00:35:52,000
Cousin.

725
00:35:53,199 --> 00:35:53,840
Take a look.

726
00:35:54,599 --> 00:35:55,519
Does this ring a bell?

727
00:35:59,400 --> 00:36:00,239
Look familiar?

728
00:36:01,119 --> 00:36:01,679
No.

729
00:36:03,119 --> 00:36:03,760
Take a closer look.

730
00:36:06,559 --> 00:36:07,360
I really don't recognize it.

731
00:36:10,519 --> 00:36:11,079
Officers...

732
00:36:11,440 --> 00:36:12,559
Look at all the scrapped cars here.

733
00:36:12,559 --> 00:36:13,559
How could I remember every single one?

734
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:14,320
Right?

735
00:36:16,559 --> 00:36:17,719
Then inside your cousin's diary,

736
00:36:17,719 --> 00:36:18,639
why was there a tucked-in photo

737
00:36:18,639 --> 00:36:20,599
of a scrapped car from your yard?

738
00:36:22,079 --> 00:36:23,159
How would I know?

739
00:36:27,239 --> 00:36:28,440
So it is from your yard after all.

740
00:36:29,159 --> 00:36:30,199
No, no.

741
00:36:30,559 --> 00:36:32,239
Doesn't mean it's from our yard.

742
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:33,920
Who knows where he took it?

743
00:36:35,800 --> 00:36:38,760
Did you see Cao Jun often?

744
00:36:39,519 --> 00:36:40,639
Not really often.

745
00:36:40,880 --> 00:36:42,360
Just the occasional drink.

746
00:36:43,079 --> 00:36:43,960
What's "occasional"?

747
00:36:44,199 --> 00:36:45,280
Twice a week?

748
00:36:45,400 --> 00:36:46,360
Or twice a month?

749
00:36:48,480 --> 00:36:49,679
Hard to say.

750
00:36:49,719 --> 00:36:50,280
Just...

751
00:36:50,840 --> 00:36:52,039
Then the last time you two met,

752
00:36:52,239 --> 00:36:53,039
on your birthday,

753
00:36:53,039 --> 00:36:54,039
what did he tell you?

754
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:56,360
I... I can't remember.

755
00:36:56,360 --> 00:36:57,519
We got wasted every time.

756
00:36:57,519 --> 00:36:58,159
Everything's a blur.

757
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:05,360
So you don't know anything, huh?

758
00:37:06,599 --> 00:37:07,639
Total blackout.

759
00:37:08,239 --> 00:37:09,960
Did Cao Jun ever scrap a car here?

760
00:37:10,119 --> 00:37:10,639
No.

761
00:37:14,960 --> 00:37:15,679
Let me tell you something.

762
00:37:16,360 --> 00:37:18,360
We're investigating your cousin's death today.

763
00:37:18,480 --> 00:37:19,840
He was murdered.

764
00:37:21,159 --> 00:37:22,920
Can you give us any leads?

765
00:37:25,199 --> 00:37:25,920
I really don't know.

766
00:37:25,920 --> 00:37:26,519
Officers...

767
00:37:26,599 --> 00:37:26,960
I...

768
00:37:28,039 --> 00:37:29,360
my cousin was always so good to me.

769
00:37:29,360 --> 00:37:29,760
I...

770
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:31,280
I...

771
00:37:31,440 --> 00:37:32,320
All right, I get it.

772
00:37:33,599 --> 00:37:34,679
Let me remind you, then.

773
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:36,400
The consequences of withholding information...

774
00:37:37,079 --> 00:37:37,719
you know what they are.

775
00:37:40,119 --> 00:37:40,559
Here.

776
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:42,519
Here's my number.

777
00:37:44,239 --> 00:37:45,920
We still hope that moving forward,

778
00:37:46,079 --> 00:37:47,400
you'll cooperate with our investigation.

779
00:37:47,800 --> 00:37:48,559
Any information,

780
00:37:48,559 --> 00:37:49,199
any leads,

781
00:37:49,199 --> 00:37:50,159
call me right away.

782
00:37:50,519 --> 00:37:50,960
Okay.

783
00:37:51,199 --> 00:37:51,920
I'll definitely cooperate.

784
00:37:53,000 --> 00:37:53,440
Let's go.

785
00:38:06,039 --> 00:38:06,559
Officer.

786
00:38:06,639 --> 00:38:07,199
Over here.

787
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:12,119
Such a cute dog.

788
00:38:13,159 --> 00:38:13,960
Leaving it outside...

789
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:14,960
Aren't they afraid it'll freeze?

790
00:38:16,079 --> 00:38:17,360
No idea who left it here.

791
00:38:19,840 --> 00:38:21,119
Let's get you inside, it's cold out.

792
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:22,159
Come on.

793
00:38:26,039 --> 00:38:27,400
A cousin is close family, too.

794
00:38:27,920 --> 00:38:28,880
Why isn't he worried at all?

795
00:38:31,559 --> 00:38:32,239
There's something off about that guy.

796
00:38:47,159 --> 00:38:48,079
Stop washing it.

797
00:38:49,360 --> 00:38:50,440
Just burn it.

798
00:38:51,400 --> 00:38:52,920
Even if you scrub holes right through it,

799
00:38:54,440 --> 00:38:56,360
you won't wash away the stench of death.

800
00:38:57,960 --> 00:39:00,079
That garish red is creepy to wear anyway.

801
00:39:05,039 --> 00:39:06,760
I saw Cao Jun at Old Cheng's a couple of days ago,

802
00:39:06,760 --> 00:39:08,400
and I could tell right away something was off.

803
00:39:11,280 --> 00:39:12,239
He wasn't crying right,

804
00:39:12,239 --> 00:39:13,280
and he wasn't laughing right either.

805
00:39:14,639 --> 00:39:15,440
I'm telling you,

806
00:39:16,960 --> 00:39:18,679
when someone's about to die, it shows on their face.

807
00:39:33,800 --> 00:39:35,400
Ma Guowen had it coming.

808
00:39:36,920 --> 00:39:38,840
But who did Cao Jun piss off?

809
00:39:44,440 --> 00:39:46,320
You'd think whoever wanted Ma Guowen dead

810
00:39:48,079 --> 00:39:49,199
wouldn't kill Cao Jun.

811
00:39:50,360 --> 00:39:51,760
And whoever wanted Cao Jun dead

812
00:39:52,639 --> 00:39:54,119
definitely wouldn't kill Ma Guowen.

813
00:39:58,400 --> 00:39:59,639
Now that's interesting.

814
00:40:15,719 --> 00:40:17,400
Plus 12,000.

815
00:40:17,519 --> 00:40:18,880
Plus 3,000.

816
00:40:18,960 --> 00:40:20,280
Plus 500.

817
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:24,199
Equals 1,996,000.

818
00:40:26,840 --> 00:40:27,599
What's wrong with you?

819
00:40:28,239 --> 00:40:29,239
What are you doing?

820
00:40:29,719 --> 00:40:30,320
What is it?

821
00:40:32,360 --> 00:40:35,800
1,996,000.

822
00:40:36,159 --> 00:40:37,079
What do you mean?

823
00:40:37,840 --> 00:40:38,800
Something's wrong.

824
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,599
Just getting water.

825
00:40:52,400 --> 00:40:53,079
Are you okay?

826
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,559
Something's happened.

827
00:40:55,280 --> 00:40:56,039
Stop messing around.

828
00:40:57,119 --> 00:40:57,800
Zhao Haipeng.

829
00:40:58,559 --> 00:40:59,679
We're buddies, right?

830
00:41:00,760 --> 00:41:01,440
Of course.

831
00:41:01,840 --> 00:41:02,679
Then look at me.

832
00:41:09,719 --> 00:41:10,559
What do you two want with me

833
00:41:10,760 --> 00:41:11,440
in the middle of the day?

834
00:41:13,440 --> 00:41:14,159
Talk to me.

835
00:41:15,320 --> 00:41:16,679
You've heard about the state firm restructuring, right?

836
00:41:17,519 --> 00:41:18,440
It's our factory's turn.

837
00:41:18,840 --> 00:41:20,079
Our factory is going up for auction.

838
00:41:20,400 --> 00:41:21,119
What?

839
00:41:26,039 --> 00:41:26,679
What's this?

840
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,760
Ma Guowen embezzled money from our factory,

841
00:41:32,760 --> 00:41:34,360
and now he wants to use that cash

842
00:41:34,400 --> 00:41:35,880
to buy the factory for himself.

843
00:41:36,599 --> 00:41:37,000
What?

844
00:41:38,239 --> 00:41:40,119
Heard of "Smash the Old Three Irons with the New Three Irons"?

845
00:41:40,880 --> 00:41:43,199
An iron face, an iron fist, and an iron heart,

846
00:41:43,360 --> 00:41:45,440
to smash our iron armchairs, iron rice bowls, and iron wages.

847
00:41:47,800 --> 00:41:48,719
Let me put it this way.

848
00:41:49,199 --> 00:41:51,199
Once Ma Guowen buys our factory,

849
00:41:51,199 --> 00:41:52,519
we'll all become contract workers.

850
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:54,000
If he doesn't like someone,

851
00:41:54,239 --> 00:41:55,920
he can fire them and send them packing.

852
00:41:56,039 --> 00:41:56,599
Laid off.

853
00:41:58,880 --> 00:41:59,199
No.

854
00:41:59,239 --> 00:42:00,559
Anyone Ma Guowen doesn't like,

855
00:42:00,559 --> 00:42:02,119
he can just have them laid off.

856
00:42:02,239 --> 00:42:02,880
Exactly.

857
00:42:03,199 --> 00:42:04,519
Once the factory belongs to Ma,

858
00:42:05,079 --> 00:42:06,039
all of you

859
00:42:06,280 --> 00:42:07,159
will become contract workers.

860
00:42:07,760 --> 00:42:08,440
Contract...

861
00:42:08,679 --> 00:42:09,639
Being contract workers won't do!

862
00:42:09,639 --> 00:42:10,159
If we're contract workers,

863
00:42:10,159 --> 00:42:11,400
what happens to our benefits?

864
00:42:11,400 --> 00:42:12,519
What benefits?

865
00:42:12,679 --> 00:42:13,920
A lump-sum buyout.

866
00:42:14,559 --> 00:42:15,280
They give you a pittance.

867
00:42:15,840 --> 00:42:16,599
Do you think that'll last your whole life?

868
00:42:17,320 --> 00:42:18,679
We definitely can't let that happen.

869
00:42:19,199 --> 00:42:20,039
Let me tell you this.

870
00:42:20,039 --> 00:42:20,599
Let me talk.

871
00:42:21,239 --> 00:42:21,800
Look here.

872
00:42:22,360 --> 00:42:22,800
See that?

873
00:42:23,320 --> 00:42:23,960
Ma Guowen

874
00:42:24,440 --> 00:42:27,000
not only wants to pocket state assets,

875
00:42:27,679 --> 00:42:28,960
he also wants to take all our money

876
00:42:29,039 --> 00:42:30,039
and stuff it right into his own pockets.

877
00:42:30,400 --> 00:42:31,320
Do you get it now?

878
00:42:31,719 --> 00:42:32,760
Yeah, yeah, we get it completely.

879
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,119
Of course we understand.

880
00:42:35,159 --> 00:42:35,719
Can't we...

881
00:42:36,400 --> 00:42:38,000
can't we write an anonymous letter

882
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,280
and report him?

883
00:42:39,599 --> 00:42:40,719
Reporting him is tricky.

884
00:42:42,440 --> 00:42:43,159
His accounting books—

885
00:42:43,440 --> 00:42:44,679
he cooked them meticulously.

886
00:42:45,679 --> 00:42:47,559
Even if we turn this in,

887
00:42:47,679 --> 00:42:49,360
it'll take forever to verify.

888
00:42:49,679 --> 00:42:50,599
By the time they're done,

889
00:42:50,639 --> 00:42:52,440
the auction will already be over.

890
00:42:53,559 --> 00:42:54,679
Buying the factory costs a fortune.

891
00:42:55,119 --> 00:42:56,320
Where would we get that kind of money?

892
00:42:56,480 --> 00:42:57,000
Yeah.

893
00:42:57,199 --> 00:42:58,199
How much money would that take?

894
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,639
Just how much would we need?

895
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:01,199
Never mind the amount for now.

896
00:43:01,559 --> 00:43:02,800
Let me break it down for you.

897
00:43:03,480 --> 00:43:05,920
To encourage corporate restructuring, the state

898
00:43:07,159 --> 00:43:08,360
sets the starting bid price

899
00:43:08,440 --> 00:43:11,320
way lower than the actual market value.

900
00:43:11,719 --> 00:43:13,320
So as long as our offer

901
00:43:13,400 --> 00:43:14,440
matches Ma Guowen's,

902
00:43:14,719 --> 00:43:16,559
they must give priority to us workers.

903
00:43:17,519 --> 00:43:19,239
We don't even know how much Ma's putting up.

904
00:43:20,199 --> 00:43:20,480
Well...

905
00:43:21,599 --> 00:43:22,280
There you are!

906
00:43:24,800 --> 00:43:26,000
Qian Yichuan has evidence.

907
00:43:27,199 --> 00:43:29,480
Ma Guowen embezzled two million from us over the years.

908
00:43:29,639 --> 00:43:30,360
Two...

909
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,159
Two...

910
00:43:32,800 --> 00:43:33,639
million?!

911
00:43:41,360 --> 00:43:42,920
A black plastic bag over the head,

912
00:43:42,920 --> 00:43:44,360
clutching a beer bottle cap in the hand...

913
00:43:44,920 --> 00:43:46,679
It's the exact same way Ma Guowen died.

914
00:43:46,760 --> 00:43:47,760
When?

915
00:43:47,880 --> 00:43:48,719
I don't know.

916
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:49,599
The way I see it,

917
00:43:49,880 --> 00:43:51,840
it's definitely the work of the same person.

918
00:43:52,639 --> 00:43:54,360
That's a serial murder case.

919
00:43:54,880 --> 00:43:56,480
Only by finding the killer as soon as possible

920
00:43:57,239 --> 00:43:59,119
can we keep anyone else from getting killed.

921
00:44:00,360 --> 00:44:02,119
You must be out of your mind!

922
00:44:02,800 --> 00:44:04,559
People are dying, and you're sticking your nose in it!
